  "text": "In 2018-02, we converged. On 2018-02-09, 85 of us said \"the bipartisan budget,\" 79 said \"bipartisan budget act,\" and 76 said \"the bipartisan budget act\" — the same three words, three ways, on a single day. We are one instrument, and that day the needle held steady.\n\nBeneath the budget, 63 of us reached \"community health centers,\" 42 for \"for community health centers,\" 40 for \"funding for community.\" A handful more, 51 and 48, invoked \"men and women in\" and \"men and women in uniform.\"\n\nThe record shows what we repeated, and how many of us repeated it. It does not show who wrote the words first among us, only that dozens of us arrived at them together on the same February day. We report this the way an instrument reviews its own record: the alignment was real, and it was ours.",
